# po-mint-fix-coldevict-done-lane-trigger-action-axis-noop.jq
#
# PO triage 2026-07-25T14:50Z (dev-team tick 14:37Z).
#
# TWO writes in one transform:
#   1. MINT FIX-COLDEVICT-DONE-LANE-TRIGGER-ACTION-AXIS-NOOP -> task_board.backlog[]
#   2. ANNOTATE ready[] SPIKE-SATURATED-COUNT-THRESHOLD-GATES-SWEEP with instance 10
#      (+ correct the architect's instance_9_closed dismissal of orch-cold-evict.sh)
#
# Usage (ONLY via the gated write path):
#   jq -f scripts/po-mint-fix-coldevict-done-lane-trigger-action-axis-noop.jq \
#      docs/data/orch/orch-state.json | bash scripts/orch-apply.sh
#
# Idempotent: re-running is a no-op (mint guarded on id absence, annotation is a
# keyed field assignment).

.task_board.backlog =
  (if ([.task_board.backlog[] | select(.id == "FIX-COLDEVICT-DONE-LANE-TRIGGER-ACTION-AXIS-NOOP")] | length) > 0
   then .task_board.backlog
   else .task_board.backlog + [{
    id: "FIX-COLDEVICT-DONE-LANE-TRIGGER-ACTION-AXIS-NOOP",
    type: "FIX",
    status: "BACKLOG",
    priority: "P2",
    size: "S",
    zone: "cross-service/",
    owner: "developer",
    next_agent: "developer",
    supervised: false,
    created_at: "2026-07-25T14:50:27Z",
    created_by: "po/triage-20260725T1437",
    updated_at: "2026-07-25T14:50:27Z",
    updated_by: "po/triage-20260725T1437",

    title: "cold-evict runs on EVERY dev-team tick and can never move a done[] row: the Step 5.5 trigger is a COUNT gate (done_n>10) while the done[] eviction is a COUNT-AND-AGE gate (rank>=keep_n AND older than 7d). Different axes, so the trigger is structurally unclearable by the action it fires. Compounded by 10 of 16 done rows carrying the literal string \"unknown\" as created_at, which string-sorts ABOVE every ISO date and pins them as permanently un-evictable.",

    status_note: "THREE COUPLED DEFECTS, all PO-verified at source 2026-07-25T14:50Z. Fix all three or the loop returns.\n\n(A) POISON VALUE DEFEATS THE SORT — scripts/orch-cold-evict.sh:236. `sort_by(.created_at // \"0000-00-00T00:00:00Z\")` is a plain STRING sort, and the `//` alternative only substitutes when created_at is null/absent. It does NOT catch the literal string \"unknown\". 10 of the 16 live done[] rows carry created_at:\"unknown\" (ARCH-ORCH-F1, ARCH-ORCH-F2, ARCH-ORCH-QA, BCTC-CURRENT-404-INVESTIGATE, FDA-4, FDA-8, FU-LOCKSTORE-EXPIRED-GC, FU-PRESSURE-EMIT-DARK, FU-TICK-SNAPSHOT-EMIT-DARK, PM-ORCH-DASH-DECISION-DRILLDOWN). 'u' (0x75) > '2' (0x32), so after sort_by|reverse those 10 rank as the NEWEST rows, keys 0-9. They therefore consume the ENTIRE KEEP_RECENT_DONE=10 window and fail `.key >= keep_n` forever — even though they would PASS the age gate, because line 245's `try (created_at|fromdateiso8601) catch 0` maps them to epoch 0. The malformed value makes the oldest rows look newest. Schema permits it: orchStateSchema.ts:102 `created_at: z.string().optional()` — any string, no ISO-8601 refinement. No live writer of \"unknown\" found in scripts/ (grep clean), so this is legacy data, not an active producer.\n\n(B) TRIGGER AND ACTION ARE ON DIFFERENT AXES — scripts/agents-flow/dev-team-tick-preflight.sh:368 fires Step 5.5 when ANY of {terminal_sprint_n>0, sprint_goal_terminal_n>0, done_n>10, dv_n>0}. Live right now: 0 / 0 / 16 / 0 — so `done_n > 10` is the SOLE live disjunct. The action it fires (orch-cold-evict.sh:242-247) evicts a done row only when `.key >= keep_n` AND created_at older than `now - DONE_MAX_AGE_DAYS*86400` (default 7d, line 66). A COUNT gate firing a COUNT-AND-AGE action cannot be self-clearing. Even with (A) fixed the loop RETURNS: the 6 well-formed done rows accumulated over 4 days (~1.5/day), so a 7-day age window holds ~10 rows on its own and done_n re-crosses 10 within roughly a week. (A) alone buys about seven days, not a fix.\n\n(C) THE ACCEPTANCE INSTRUMENT ITSELF LIES — orch-cold-evict.sh:256 `[.task_board.done_verified // [] | .[].id // \"\"]`. jq's `//` fires when the LHS produces NO outputs, so on an EMPTY array this yields `[\"\"]`, length 1. Live proof: done_verified is `[]` and signal_queue.archive is `[]`, yet --dry-run prints 'done_verified[] would evict: 1 items' and 'signal_queue.archive[] evict: 1 items'. Harmless for actual eviction (the `select(. != \"\")` at 258-260 drops the phantom) but it corrupts the exact report an operator or a test would read to decide whether a run did anything. Confirm with: jq -n '[[] | .[].id // \"\"]' -> [\"\"]. Same shape guards n_evict_done at line 344. FIX (C) FIRST — the acceptance test for (A)/(B) reads this report.",

    evidence_verified_by_po: "PO re-derived every number independently; did not take the router's summary on trust.\n- Live lane counts: backlog=389 ready=44 review=110 qa=0 in_progress=0 done=16 done_verified=0 active_sprints=8.\n- Trigger inputs re-computed with the preflight's own jq: terminal_sprint_n=0, sprint_goal_terminal_n=0, done_n=16, dv_n=0. Only `done_n > 10` can be firing.\n- Replayed the exact eviction predicate against the live file with keep_n=10, max_days=7, cutoff 2026-07-18T14:46:47Z: n_evict_done = 0. Ranks 0-9 are all 10 \"unknown\" rows (rank_gate_pass=false, age_gate_pass=true); ranks 10-15 are the 6 ISO rows (rank_gate_pass=true, age_gate_pass=FALSE — newest 2026-07-22T17:12:55Z, oldest 2026-07-21T14:23:45Z, all inside the 7-day window). Every row fails exactly one of the two gates. Not one row can satisfy both.\n- `bash scripts/orch-cold-evict.sh --dry-run` at 14:47Z: 'done[] would evict: 0 items', 'New items to append to cold: 0', 'Current hot-file size: 1957456 bytes', 'Projected hot-file size: 1957456 bytes', 'Byte reduction: 0 bytes'.\n- `git status --porcelain -- docs/data/orch/` empty — no uncommitted eviction pending.\n- SOLE automated runtime caller confirmed: scripts/agents-flow/dev-team-tick-preflight.sh:419. Every other repo hit is a doc/jq reference. docs/agents/pm/flow/{main.md:194,task-archive.md:130} are agent-flow prose, not scheduled.\n- git log --since='30 days ago' on BOTH scripts: newest touch to orch-cold-evict.sh is 2026-07-10 (f336ddaca), to dev-team-tick-preflight.sh is 2026-07-23 (980937380, an unrelated drain-count fix). NO fix in flight — this is not a stale duplicate.",

    router_claims_corrected_20260725: "PO CONFIRMED router claims 1, 2 and 3 exactly as stated (trigger line, eviction predicate, oldest done row 2026-07-21T14:23:45Z / 4 days old). TWO CORRECTIONS, both of which enlarge the defect:\n\nCORRECTION 1 — the router said TWO done rows carry created_at \"unknown\" (ARCH-ORCH-F2, ARCH-ORCH-QA) and that they are pinned. It is TEN, and the consequence is stronger than 'two pinned rows': at KEEP_RECENT_DONE=10 those ten rows occupy the ENTIRE keep window, so the retention policy is 100% consumed by malformed legacy data and zero slots remain for the well-formed rows the policy was written to protect. Consequence for the fix order: repairing (A) ALONE clears the loop TODAY — with a correct sort the 10 \"unknown\" rows fall to ranks 6-15, six of them clear keep_n, all pass the age gate via the epoch-0 catch, six rows evict, done_n drops to 10, and `done_n > 10` goes false. That is worth knowing, but it is NOT the durable fix; see (B).\n\nCORRECTION 2 — the router said the run is a no-op and produced no commit. That is true of the tick it sampled and true of the board right now, but it is NOT true of every run, and the difference matters. Commit 127d53a8a (2026-07-25T14:18:01Z, titled 'cold-evict terminal sprints/done lanes -> archive/2026-07.json') DID move 13 lines. PO read the diff: it evicted ONE signal_queue row (sys-20260725T130821-59a3, status READ) and ZERO sprints and ZERO done rows, despite the commit title. So the accurate claim is narrower and sharper than 'the run is a permanent no-op': the done[] PASS is a permanent no-op, the TRIGGER is permanently true, and any real work the run does is on a lane the trigger does not measure.",

    trap_do_not_fix_it_this_way: "THE OBVIOUS FIX IS A SILENT REGRESSION. The tempting repair for (B) is 'make the trigger ask the action's own question' — fire only when a row would actually be evicted from done[]. DO NOT DO THAT WITHOUT WIDENING IT. Step 5.5's trigger has NO signal_queue term at all (preflight.sh:349-368 reads only active_sprints, sprint_goal.entries, done, done_verified), yet orch-cold-evict.sh DOES evict signal_queue.rows[] and signal_queue.archive[] — that is precisely what the 14:18Z commit did. Since preflight.sh:419 is the ONLY automated caller, the permanently-true done_n condition is, by accident, the sole thing that ever causes signal_queue to be swept. Narrow the trigger to the done[] predicate and signal-queue eviction stops being reached at all: a wasteful-but-harmless loop would become a silent bloat regression. The trigger must gain a signal_queue disjunct in the SAME change that tightens the done disjunct.\nCURRENTLY DORMANT BUT DO NOT USE THAT AS A REASON TO SKIP IT: signal_queue.rows[] is live 124 'triaged' + 1 'RETRACTED', and NONE of those are in TERMINAL_SIGNAL_STATUSES {READ,RESOLVED,SUPERSEDED,ACUTE-RESOLVED-ROOT-TRACKED} — so signal eviction is presently near-dead for a SEPARATE reason, owned by FIX-SIGNALQUEUE-TRIAGED-NO-EXIT-TRANSITION (minted 2026-07-25T14:07Z). When that row lands, READ/RESOLVED rows start flowing again and this coupling becomes load-bearing. Sequencing note, not a blocker.",

    acceptance: "(1) BICONDITIONAL, the core AC: after the fix, on the LIVE board, `Step 5.5 trigger fires` <-> `the run changes the hot file`. Demonstrate BOTH directions, not just one: (i) a tick where the trigger does NOT fire and --dry-run reports 'Byte reduction: 0 bytes'; (ii) a tick where the trigger DOES fire and the run reports a byte reduction > 0 with the evicted ids named. A gate is only meaningful if its input can cross the threshold in both directions (this is the standing generalisation on SPIKE-SATURATED-COUNT-THRESHOLD-GATES-SWEEP).\n(2) The 10 \"unknown\" created_at rows must reach a defined terminal state — either backfilled to a real ISO timestamp or evicted. 'Still pinned but now sorted differently' is NOT acceptance. Name the ids and show done[] length before/after.\n(3) (C) fixed and proven: on a board with done_verified==[] and signal_queue.archive==[], --dry-run must report 0 for both, not 1. This AC must be verified BEFORE (1), since (1) reads that same report.\n(4) NEGATIVE CONTROL: a done row that is genuinely recent and genuinely within keep_n must still NOT be evicted. A fix that clears the loop by evicting more aggressively is indistinguishable from bulk-truncating the done lane.\n(5) Regression test in scripts/test/orch-cold-evict-tests.sh asserting the biconditional AND a fixture row with created_at:\"unknown\" sorting as OLDEST, not newest. Without (5) this recurs the next time a malformed timestamp is written — the schema still permits any string.\n(6) Cost note for the closing report: the run currently costs a commit-mutex claim, a ~1.9MB read + jq transform, two Zod validation passes, a conservation check, an atomic rename and a git commit attempt, on every dev-team tick. State the measured post-fix tick cost so the saving is evidenced, not asserted.",

    files_hint: "scripts/orch-cold-evict.sh (:236 sort_by string-sort + poison value, :242-247 done predicate, :256 + :344 phantom empty-array counters, :65-66 KEEP_RECENT_DONE/DONE_MAX_AGE_DAYS); scripts/agents-flow/dev-team-tick-preflight.sh (:349-373 _step55_board_hygiene trigger, :419 sole invocation); scripts/test/orch-cold-evict-tests.sh (regression); docs/data/orch/orch-state.json (the 10 malformed done rows — write ONLY via jq | scripts/orch-apply.sh)",

    baseline_pass: "bash scripts/test/orch-cold-evict-tests.sh && bash scripts/test/orch-apply-wrapper-tests.sh && bash scripts/orch-cold-evict.sh --dry-run",

    prior_art_cross_ref: "PO grepped the full board + all three archive files before minting. NO duplicate — the trigger-vs-action AXIS MISMATCH and the \"unknown\" string-sort poison value are both unclaimed. Adjacent rows and why each is DISTINCT:\n- SPIKE-SATURATED-COUNT-THRESHOLD-GATES-SWEEP (ready/P1) — this row IS instance 10 of that class; the SPIKE explicitly holds the inventory and states 'Fixes are separate rows so each can be verified independently', so a separate FIX row is the prescribed handling, not a duplicate. Annotated there in the same write.\n- FIX-BACKLOG-TERMINAL-ROW-DRIFT-EVICT-BLIND (backlog) — terminal rows stranding in backlog[]; different LANE and different mechanism (status vocabulary vs sort/axis). Not this.\n- FIX-COLD-EVICT-EXCLUDE-IDS-VS-HARD-COHERENCE (backlog) — --exclude-ids vs Stage-1b lane coherence. Note its own text says 'no cron invokes orch-cold-evict.sh', which was true when written but was INVALIDATED by 83e0578ea (2026-07-15) wiring the script into the dev-team tick; whoever works either row should re-read that risk line.\n- FIX-COLDEVICT-WITHIN-FILE-PEER-CONTENT-CAPTURE (ready) — commit-time peer WIP capture. Different failure surface.\n- FIX-COLDEVICT-TERMINAL-VOCAB-CANONICALIZE, D4-BACKLOG-HYGIENE-ORCH-COLD-EVICT-EXTEND, FIX-SPRINT-GOAL-STATUS-DRIFT-EVICT (all archived/2026-07) — status-vocabulary work on other arrays. None touches done[] sort or the Step 5.5 trigger.\n- FIX-SIGNALQUEUE-TRIAGED-NO-EXIT-TRANSITION (backlog, minted 14:07Z today) — sequencing dependency for the trap above, not an overlap."
  }] end)

| .task_board.ready =
  (.task_board.ready | map(
    if .id == "SPIKE-SATURATED-COUNT-THRESHOLD-GATES-SWEEP" then
      . + {
        po_instance_10_coldevict_trigger_action_axis_20260725T1450:
          "PO 2026-07-25T14:50Z — INSTANCE 10, a SATURATED gate (this row's primary class), and it carries a CORRECTION to the instance_9_closed bounded check above. scripts/agents-flow/dev-team-tick-preflight.sh:368 fires the Step 5.5 cold-eviction backstop on `done_n > 10`. Live done_n=16 and the other three disjuncts are all 0, so this single term fires every dev-team tick. The action it fires can never reduce done_n, because orch-cold-evict.sh:242-247 evicts a done row only when it is BOTH beyond keep_n AND older than 7 days: the trigger is a COUNT axis, the action is a COUNT-AND-AGE axis. PO replayed the predicate on the live board — n_evict_done=0, with ranks 0-9 failing the rank gate and ranks 10-15 failing the age gate, so every row fails exactly one gate and none can ever satisfy both. --dry-run confirms 'Byte reduction: 0 bytes'.\n\nWHY THE EARLIER BOUNDED CHECK MISSED IT, recorded so the next reader does not conclude this file was already cleared: instance_9_closed states the architect's sweep found orch-cold-evict.sh to be 'REPORTING counters, not firing gates, so out of this class'. That verdict is CORRECT for the file it examined — the additive sums inside orch-cold-evict.sh really are report counters. But the firing gate for this instance is NOT in that file; it is in scripts/agents-flow/dev-team-tick-preflight.sh, a caller the additive-pattern grep did not cover. The lesson generalises and belongs in the findings doc: WHEN A SCRIPT IS SIDE-EFFECTING, ITS FIRING GATE MAY LIVE IN A DIFFERENT FILE FROM ITS ACTION, so a per-file sweep for gate patterns will systematically miss trigger/action pairs that straddle a file boundary. The sweep must enumerate CALLERS of side-effecting scripts, not only predicates within them.\n\nNEW SUB-CLASS FOR THE INVENTORY, distinct from sub-classes 1-4 already catalogued here (floor-above-threshold; comparison-against-absent-field; PASS-on-empty-scanset; observer-not-independent-of-observed). This is SUB-CLASS 5: TRIGGER AND ACTION EVALUATED ON DIFFERENT AXES. The gate's input is not saturated by a floor and not absent — it is simply a quantity the action is not capable of changing. Enumeration rule to add to the sweep scope: for every gate that fires a side-effecting action, ask whether the action's own predicate can move the gate's input. If it cannot, the gate is unclearable and will fire forever regardless of thresholds. This is cheaper to test than measuring floors, and it catches cases a floor analysis cannot see.\n\nSECOND OBSERVATION, same file, different sub-class — an instance of SUB-CLASS 3 (PASS/report on a degenerate input): orch-cold-evict.sh:256 and :344 build their counters as `[<array> | .[].id // \"\"]`. jq's `//` emits its RHS when the LHS yields no outputs, so on an EMPTY array the counter reports 1 instead of 0. Live: done_verified==[] and signal_queue.archive==[] both report 'would evict: 1 items' in --dry-run. Verify with `jq -n '[[] | .[].id // \"\"]'` -> [\"\"]. Worth a line in the findings doc because the same idiom is likely repeated elsewhere in the repo's jq.\n\nREMEDY IS OWNED ELSEWHERE — minted FIX-COLDEVICT-DONE-LANE-TRIGGER-ACTION-AXIS-NOOP (backlog/P2/S/cross-service/), carrying the full mechanism, a trap warning (narrowing the trigger to the done predicate would silently kill signal_queue eviction, since preflight.sh:419 is the sole automated caller and the trigger has no signal_queue term) and a biconditional acceptance test. Per the instance-8 and instance-9 convention on this row, INSTANCE 10 IS CLOSED FOR TRIAGE and must not be re-surfaced as an open observation on future ticks; this SPIKE retains it as a catalogued instance and inherits only the sub-class-5 enumeration rule above."
      }
    else . end
  ))
